**.idea/

# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
**target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
**Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk


# Added by cargo
**docs/
**.claude/

.superpowers/

# Model artifacts are dev-time downloads and stay untracked — EXCEPT the
# vendored VAD model, which is COMMITTED so CI and every clone have it with no
# download step (1.1 MiB; see NOTICE sections 1-2 for its MIT provenance).
# Re-including a path under an excluded directory needs the parent re-included
# first, hence the `Models/*` / `!dir/` / `dir/*` ladder rather than a bare
# `Models/`. Everything else under Models/ — including vadkit's own
# `.cache/huggingface/` download bookkeeping — stays ignored.
Models/*
!Models/vadkit/
Models/vadkit/*
!Models/vadkit/silero-vad-unified-256ms-v6.2.1.mlmodelc/
